{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For the life of the flesh is in the blood, and I have given it to you upon the altar</b>. The meaning of this verse is that He says that blood is forbidden to us because He has given it to us to be upon the altar to make atonement for our lives, and it is the portion of HaShem, like the meaning of the fat. And if one objects: why did He forbid the blood of the wild animal and the bird, which are not brought as offerings — we reject the questioner's premise, for He wished to distance us from all blood so that we would not go astray with it, even though He did not do so with fat, because fat is recognizable [as non-blood]. And the Rav wrote in the Guide for the Perplexed (III:46) that the Chaldeans abhorred blood and considered it an impurity, but those who wished to commune with demons and to divine the future from them would eat of it, and the Torah always aims to demolish the structures of their folly by reversing their ideas, and therefore it forbade blood in consumption and chose it for purification through sprinkling and to cast it upon the altar for atonement. And therefore He said (Leviticus 17:10), 'And I will set My face against the soul that eats the blood,' just as He said concerning one who gives of his seed to Molech (Leviticus 20:6), which involves bringing [worship to] a species of idolatry, for this is not said regarding any other commandment. And these matters are well-reasoned, but the verses do not indicate thus, for they always state the reason for the prohibition as 'for the life of all flesh is its blood' (Leviticus 17:14), 'for the life of the flesh is in the blood' (Leviticus 17:11), and He repeated in the recapitulation of the Torah (Deuteronomy 12:23), 'Only be strong not to eat the blood, for the blood is the life, and you shall not eat the life with the flesh.' And the proper interpretation of the reason for its prohibition is that HaShem created all lower creatures for the needs of man, for he alone among them recognizes his Creator, and even so, He did not initially permit them for consumption anything except plant life, not beings possessing a soul, as stated in the portion of Genesis, where it is written (Genesis 1:29), 'Behold, I have given you every herb yielding seed,' etc. And when the Flood came, in which he was saved by the merit of Noah, and he offered sacrifices from them and they found favor, He permitted slaughter to them, as He said (ibid. 9:3), 'Every creeping thing that is alive shall be food for you; as the green herb I have given you all.' For their life exists on account of man. Now He permitted their body, which lives on account of man, to be for man's benefit and need, and [decreed] that the soul within them serve as atonement for man through the offerings before Him, may He be blessed — not that they should eat it, for it is not fitting for one who possesses a soul to eat a soul, for all souls belong to El — the soul of man and the soul of the beast are His, and one fate befalls them; as the death of one, so the death of the other, and they all have one spirit (Ecclesiastes 3:19). And according to the way the investigators among the Greeks saw it, from the Active Intellect there flashed a radiance and a very bright and luminous brilliance, and from it there went forth the spark of the animal soul. Now it is a complete soul, on a lower level. Therefore it possesses awareness to flee from harm and to pursue what is agreeable to it, and recognition of those familiar to it and love for them, like the love of dogs for their masters and remarkable recognition of the members of their masters' household, and similarly pigeons possess awareness and recognition. It is further well known that what is eaten is assimilated into the body of the eater and they become one flesh, and if a man eats the life of all flesh and it becomes joined with his blood and they become unified in the heart, there will be coarseness and grossness in the soul of man, and it will revert to being close to the nature of the animal soul that was in what was eaten, for blood does not require digestion like other foods that are transformed in their digestion, and the soul of man would hang upon the blood of the animal. And Scripture says (ibid. ibid. 21), 'Who knows the spirit of man, whether it goes upward, and the spirit of the beast, whether it goes downward to the earth.' And therefore He said (Leviticus 17:14), 'For the life of all flesh is its blood,' for all flesh, in man and in beast, has a life in the blood, and it is not fitting to mix the perishing soul with the enduring soul; rather, it shall make atonement upon the altar, as a pleasing [offering] before HaShem. And this is the reason for 'Therefore I said to the children of Israel' — because the blood is the life and it is not fitting that the soul eat the soul, and I had compassion upon the soul of man and gave it to them upon the altar, so that the soul of the beast may make atonement for his soul. And they taught in the Sifrei (see 76), 'Only be strong not to eat the blood' (Deuteronomy 12:23) — Rabbi Judah says: this teaches that they were drenched in blood, etc. 'For the blood is the life' (ibid.) — to declare what caused it. 'And you shall not eat the life with the flesh' (ibid.) — this is a limb from a living animal. This is a hint and proof for what we have explained. And therefore He further commanded (Leviticus 17:13) to cover all blood of the wild animal and the bird, for their blood is not brought upon the altar, for even among birds only two species are brought, and even they are not slaughtered [by slaughtering], but among domesticated animals the majority of those commonly found are slaughtered to the Name of the Great One and their blood makes atonement, and it is not fitting to cover it. And He did not require covering the blood of unconsecrated slaughter in a domesticated animal because there is no unconsecrated [slaughter] in the wilderness, and even afterwards He will command concerning the majority."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:55:15.532472155Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}